@meta
id: 16-07
title: Drill — bounce
chapter: 16
type: drill
skills: buffer-switch
par: 85
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl-Tab, Ctrl-Tab, Ctrl-Tab
open: order.repository.ts order.entity.ts
vimrc: set hidden

@brief
Eight times: the entity gains `note?: string;` directly under `total`,
and the repository maps it with `note: record.note ?? undefined,`
directly under its own `total` line. You start in the repository.

`hidden` is on, so no writing between hops; `:bn` there, `Ctrl-^`
back, `:wqa` at the end. Two edits, one bounce, done.

@keys
| `:bn` | to the entity |
| `Ctrl-^` | back to the repository |
| `:wqa` | write both, quit |

@hints
`:bn`, `/total`, `o`, the field, `Esc`, `Ctrl-^`, `/total`, `o`, the
mapping, `Esc`, `:wqa`.
--
The bounce is one chord. If you find yourself typing `:b` for it, stop
and use the chord; the whole point of the drill is that the way back is
free.

@solution
    :bn<Enter>  /total<Enter>  o note?: string; <Esc>
    Ctrl-^  /total<Enter>  o note: record.note ?? undefined, <Esc>  :wqa<Enter>

Seventy-odd keystrokes, of which the switching costs five.

`hidden` is doing quiet work here: the entity is modified when you
leave it, and vim lets you go because it can keep the buffer in memory
with the change. At the end `:wqa` writes both. If you ever want to see
what the option saved you, `:ls` mid-drill shows the entity as `#h +`:
alternate, hidden, modified.

@start order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}

@expected order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      note: record.note ?? undefined,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}

@start order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  note?: string;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';
